IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s334-interpretation`
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], s 341 (שיעורים מופחתים, reduced rates) and the National Insurance
-- (Reduced Rates of Insurance Contributions) Order, 5759-1999. Row IL-34, priority 2.
-- `src:N` is line N of the Law's deposited text; `ext:[order-5759] N` is line N of the Order's
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/national-insurance-reduced-rates-of-insurance-contributions-order-5759-1999.he.wiki.txt,
-- sha256 f91c3b20909bdd67e3c6135554449a0f9f393e4db732470ece542c2a72f0f007, Wikisource revision 2925120 of 2025-05-13).
--
-- WHAT THEY SAY. Section 341 is a power: the Minister, with the Finance Committee's approval, may by order fix
-- reduced rates for part of an insured person's income, or apply reduced rates to income up to a sum the order
-- names. Its last limb carries the old orders forward: what an order in force before 1.1.2006 provided on "the
-- amount of wage or income not exceeding half the average wage" now provides on the amount "not exceeding the
-- reduced collection threshold". The only order this row has is the Order of 5759-1999, whose s 1 fixes that
-- amount, for each month of a quarter and for a quarter, by the average wage of the quarter's first month.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT HERE. The Order fixes an AMOUNT, not a rate: the reduced rates themselves are Schedule J's (row
-- IL-04). The amount since 1.1.2026 is s 334(a)'s, which moves only on 1 January, so the "first month of the
-- quarter" rule gives the year's figure in every quarter and no answer anywhere differs from row IL-04's. For
-- 1999 to 2005 the Order's amount is half the average wage of the first month, and the monthly series of the
-- average wage is not deposited; for 2006 to 2025 the amount was 60% of it (the Order's own note) and the same
-- series is not deposited: NEEDS A SOURCE. Before 1999 the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987 governed; not deposited.

§ `Section 341 and the Order of 5759-1999`

§§ `Section 341: the power, and what an order needs to be validly made`

-- src:3654 | סעיף 341 – שיעורים מופחתים [תיקון: תשנ״ח־7, תשס״ה־6, תשפ״ה־7]
-- src:3655 | על אף הוראות סעיפים 337 ו־340 רשאי השר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, לקבוע בצו שיעורים מופחתים של דמי ביטוח לגבי חלק מהכנסתו של מבוטח שהוא עובד עצמאי או שהוא עובד או של מבוטח שאינו עובד ואינו עובד עצמאי, או להחיל שיעורים מופחתים על הכנסה של מבוטח כאמור שלא תעלה על סכום שיקבע בצו; הוראות לפי סעיף זה, שהיו בתוקף לפני יום א׳ בטבת התשס״ו (1 בינואר 2006) לענין קביעת סכום השכר או ההכנסה שאינם עולים על מחצית השכר הממוצע, יחולו לענין קביעת סכום השכר או ההכנסה שאינם עולים על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת.
-- src:3656 | [note: פורסם צו הביטוח הלאומי (שיעורים מופחתים של דמי ביטוח), התשנ״ט–1999.]

@ref National Insurance Law s 341 (source line 3655)
GIVEN o IS AN `An order under section 341`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 341 — the order is validly made` o MEANS
        o's `made by the Minister`
    AND o's `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset`

§§ `The Order: when it applies, and to whom`

-- ext:[order-5759] 14 | סעיף 1 – שיעור מופחת של דמי ביטוח [תיקון: תש״ס]
-- ext:[order-5759] 15 | סכום השכר או ההכנסה שאינם עולים על מחצית השכר הממוצע לעובד, לעובד עצמאי ולמבוטח שאינו עובד ואינו עובד עצמאי, ייקבע לגבי כל חודש ברבעון ולגבי רבעון, לפי הענין, לפי השכר הממוצע של החודש הראשון שבאותו רבעון; לענין זה, ”רבעון“ – כהגדרתו בלוח י״א.
-- ext:[order-5759] 16 | [note: לפי סעיף 341 סיפה לחוק הביטוח הלאומי [נוסח משולב], התשנ״ה–1995, כפי שתוקן בסעיף 66 לחוק לתיקון פקודת מס הכנסה (מס׳ 147), התשס״ה–2005, סעיף זה יחול גם לענין קביעת סכום השכר או ההכנסה שאינם עולים על 60% מהשכר הממוצע.]
-- ext:[order-5759] 18 | סעיף 2 – ביטול
-- ext:[order-5759] 19 | צו הביטוח הלאומי (שיעורים מופחתים של דמי ביטוח) (מס׳ 2), התשמ״ז–1987 – בטל מיום תחילתו של צו זה.
-- ext:[order-5759] 21 | סעיף 3 – תחילה ותחולה
-- ext:[order-5759] 22 | תחילתו של צו זה ביום י״ב בטבת התשנ״ט (1 בינואר 1999) (להלן – יום התחילה), והוא יחול על דמי ביטוח המשתלמים בעד יום התחילה ולאחריו.
-- ext:[order-5759] 24 | סעיף 4 – הוראת שעה
-- ext:[order-5759] 25 | בתקופה שמיום התחילה עד יום כ״ד באדר ב׳ התש״ס (31 במרס 2000), יחול האמור בתקנה [note: [צ״ל: בסעיף]] 1 גם לגבי עובד.

-- s 3: the Order began on 1 January 1999 and applies to contributions payable for that day and after.
@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 3 (order line 22)
GIVETH A DATE
`Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the day it began` MEANS
    YMD 1999 1 1

-- Version 0.1.1 (fid-il-34, C013): whether the Order applies to a day before its start is answered no, from art 3 alone. What governed that day (the Order No. 2 of
-- 5747-1987, not deposited) is needed only for the AMOUNT of a month, which stays refused.
@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 3 (order line 22); the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987 is not deposited
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited` MEANS
    REFUSE "contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited"

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 3 (order line 22)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` d MEANS
    Day d AT LEAST Day (`Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the day it began`)

-- s 1 names an employee, a self-employed person and one who is neither. Its heading carries the amendment
-- tag of 5760 (Kovetz HaTakanot 5760 p. 778, which is not deposited), and s 4 says that from 1.1.1999 to
-- 31.3.2000 s 1 applies also to an employee. The deposited s 1 names the employee outright, and the commencement
-- day of the amendment is not in the text: from 1.4.2000 on the deposited s 1 is followed (assumption A7).
-- So the Order reaches all three classes from 1.1.1999, and s 4 is, for an employee, the reach by that section alone
-- for the first fifteen months.
@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 4 (order line 25)
GIVETH A DATE
`Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — the last day of the temporary provision` MEANS
    YMD 2000 3 31

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 3 and s 4 (order lines 22, 25)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` d MEANS
        Day d AT LEAST Day (`Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the day it began`)
    AND Day d AT MOST  Day (`Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — the last day of the temporary provision`)

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15), s 3 and s 4
GIVEN c IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Order of 5759-1999 — the Order's amount applies to` c `on the day` d MEANS
    IF `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` d
    THEN CONSIDER c
         WHEN `an employee`                                                       THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a self-employed person`                                            THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE

§§ `The Order's amount: for a month and for a quarter`

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15); s 341 last limb (source line 3655)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Order's amount from 1999 to 2005 is half the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Order's amount from 1999 to 2005 is half the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited"

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 note (order line 16); s 341 last limb (source line 3655)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Order's amount from 2006 to 2025 is 60% of the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Order's amount from 2006 to 2025 is 60% of the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited"

@ref Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"

-- The amount for a month: the figure of the quarter's first month. Since 1.1.2026 that is s 334(a)'s reduced
-- collection threshold, which is updated only on 1 January, so it is the year's figure for all twelve months.
-- Row IL-04 answers 2026 with the published 7,703 and declines 2027 on by name; this rule asks it.
@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15); s 341 last limb (source line 3655); s 334(a) (source line 3605)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the month` GREATER THAN 12 THEN `a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 2026 THEN `s 334(a) — the reduced collection threshold for a month in` `the year`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 2006 THEN `the Order's amount from 2006 to 2025 is 60% of the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 1999 THEN `the Order's amount from 1999 to 2005 is half the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited`
           OTHERWISE `contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited`

@ref Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a quarter begins in month 1, 4, 7 or 10` MEANS
    REFUSE "a quarter begins in month 1, 4, 7 or 10"

-- The Order's own rule, for the years the threshold was a share of the average wage: half of it until 31.12.2005, and from 1.1.2006
-- 60% of it, which is how s 341's last limb read until the 2025 Budget-year Law replaced "60% of the average wage" by "the reduced
-- collection threshold" from 1.1.2026 (that Law s 19(3), Sefer HaChukim 3384 p. 396, deposited in ../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/
-- 25_lsr_6133485.pdf, sha256 eba7e1fa...ecfa). The average wage of the quarter's first month is an input: its monthly series is not
-- deposited. Nothing is rounded: the Order does not say to round (the Institute's 2025 figure 7,522 is 60% of 12,536 = 7,521.6, rounded).
@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15); s 341 last limb (source line 3655); 2025 Budget-year Law s 19(3)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage of the quarter's first month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` `the average wage of the quarter's first month` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the month` GREATER THAN 12 THEN `a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 2026 THEN `s 334(a) — the reduced collection threshold for a month in` `the year`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 2006 THEN 60% TIMES `the average wage of the quarter's first month`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 1999 THEN 50% TIMES `the average wage of the quarter's first month`
           OTHERWISE `contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited`

@ref NOTES.md fork O1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Order's s 1 does not say how a quarter's amount relates to a month's` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Order's s 1 does not say how a quarter's amount relates to a month's"

-- The amount for a quarter, at a reading. A quarter's amount is NOT the month's: the Order fixes it "for a
-- quarter" by the same average wage, and says no more (fork O1).
@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15); NOTES.md fork O1
GIVEN `the quarter's first month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
      r IS A `A reading of the Order's amount for a quarter`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` `the quarter's first month` `of` `the year` `, reading a quarter's amount as` r MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the quarter's first month` EQUALS 1 OR `the quarter's first month` EQUALS 4
            OR `the quarter's first month` EQUALS 7 OR `the quarter's first month` EQUALS 10)
    THEN `a quarter begins in month 1, 4, 7 or 10`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER r
        WHEN `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` THEN 3 TIMES (`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` `the quarter's first month` `of` `the year`)
        WHEN `a quarter's amount is declined`              THEN `the Order's s 1 does not say how a quarter's amount relates to a month's`

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15); NOTES.md fork O1 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)
GIVETH A `A reading of the Order's amount for a quarter`
`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the reading this row takes of a quarter's amount` MEANS `a quarter's amount is declined`

@ref Order of 5759-1999 s 1 (order line 15)
GIVEN `the quarter's first month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` `the quarter's first month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` `the quarter's first month` `of` `the year` `, reading a quarter's amount as` (`Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the reading this row takes of a quarter's amount`)
